WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.981
Review sheet.

2
00:00:01.261 --> 00:00:10.968
Counting tables grow as V to the power of the context length; embeddings and a neural network share statistical strength across contexts (Bengio et al.

3
00:00:11.248 --> 00:00:12.571
, 2003).

4
00:00:12.851 --> 00:00:21.021
Shapes: (N, 3) integers, (N, 3, d) embeddings, (N, 3d) concatenated, (N, H) hidden, (N, V) logits.

5
00:00:21.301 --> 00:00:27.061
Cross-entropy should be computed with log-sum-exp, and its gradient is softmax minus one-hot.

6
00:00:27.341 --> 00:00:33.443
Minibatch gradients are unbiased and noisy; sweep learning rates exponentially to find a good one.

7
00:00:33.723 --> 00:00:36.581
Train fits, dev chooses, test reports, once.

8
00:00:36.861 --> 00:00:41.683
Close train and dev losses mean underfitting; a widening gap means overfitting.

9
00:00:41.963 --> 00:00:45.696
Next week: what goes wrong inside deeper networks, and how to fix it.
